# Windows installer

NSIS assisted installer is branded desktop-owned packaging: `build/installer.nsh` may contain `customWelcomePage` / `customUnWelcomePage` / `customHeader` (GUI pages) plus the narrow `customInit` registry cleanup defined in the feature card — no MessageBox / Section / RequestExecutionLevel / customInstall, so silent `/S`, overwrite upgrade and the SHA512SUMS updater flow stay intact. `customUnWelcomePage` replaces the template's bare `MUI_UNPAGE_WELCOME`, so it must re-insert that page and re-define `MUI_WELCOMEPAGE_TITLE_3LINES` (MUI2 unsets welcome settings per page; otherwise the un-welcome title's third line clips). Keep `oneClick:false`, directory choose, per-user default path, shortcuts, and artifact `Whale-Isle-Setup-${version}.exe` (release.yml globs depend on it). Bitmaps are fixed-geometry 24-bit BMPs (sidebar 164×314, header 150×57) regenerated via `npm run installer:assets` from `scripts/render-installer-assets.js`; palette mirrors the **official light tokens** (launcher-aligned): sidebar fill `rgb(249,250,251)`, bg-base white, label primary/secondary/tertiary ink, brand blue `rgb(65,118,230)` as thin accent only, hairline `rgba(0,0,0,.10)`. Sidebar brand stack = whale + product name `Whale Isle`; uninstaller = muted grayscale of the same light composition. No near-black `#0b0d12` marketing panel, no `--boot-*` instrument canvas — no second skin. Uninstall must not delete `userData` (dsh-home). `deleteAppDataOnUninstall` / `perMachine` stay unset.

Release acceptance follows [the release process](../../docs/handbook/modules/release-process.md). Packaged smoke runs once between dist and upload; preserve and classify failures before retrying. Candidate preflight requires shipping-platform and shared CI. Promotion verifies the frozen plan, immutable installed-acceptance record and original Setup/DMG bytes; no rebuild. macOS is optional to ship, but its CI and installed acceptance are mandatory when a DMG is included. The complete case library is selected by core plus change impact.

